title: The negotiating team
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_negotiations
view-if: negotiations_timer <= 0 and seeking_government = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; negotiations_timer = 1

= The negotiating team

Antonio Hernando, Meritxell Batet, José Enrique Serrano, Jordi Sevilla, Rodolfo Ares and María Luisa Carcedo wait for instructions. Who do they sit down with this month?

- @podemos: Podemos: work towards a government agreement
- @cs: Ciudadanos: work towards a reform agreement
- @both: Both at once: try for a three-way arrangement
- @pnv_cc: The PNV and Coalición Canaria
- @catalans: Sound out ERC and Convergència
- @easy_discard

@podemos
on-arrival: up_talks += 1; rel_up += 8; rel_cs -= 4; progressives_dissent -= 5; regional_leaders_dissent += 5; institutionalists_dissent += 3

Podemos's team arrives with a 98-page document and a list of ministries. [? if up_talks >= 2 : The talks are now serious enough to sign something, if you want to. ?]

@cs
on-arrival: cs_talks += 1; rel_cs += 8; rel_up -= 5; modernisers_dissent -= 4; institutionalists_dissent -= 2; progressives_dissent += 5; trade_unionists_dissent += 2

Albert Rivera's negotiators want labour-market flexibility, an end to the provincial councils and a hard line on Catalonia. [? if cs_talks >= 2 : An agreement is within reach. ?]

@both
on-arrival: up_talks += 0.5; cs_talks += 0.5; rel_up += 3; rel_cs += 3; sanchez_authority += 2; regional_leaders_dissent += 2

Podemos will not share a table with Ciudadanos, and Ciudadanos will not sit in a government with Podemos. Your team shuttles between rooms. It makes you look like the centre of every solution, and it makes everyone suspicious of you.

@pnv_cc
on-arrival: rel_pnv += 8; rel_cc += 8

The PNV wants its fiscal arrangements respected and transfers of powers to Euskadi; Coalición Canaria wants the islands' economic regime. Both are small, both are reliable, and both know what their votes are worth.

@catalans
on-arrival: rel_erc += 8; rel_junts += 6; sanchez_authority -= 1; regional_leaders_dissent += 10 if red_lines = 1; federal_committee_balance -= 4 if red_lines = 1

ERC's spokesman repeats that their price is a referendum. [? if red_lines = 1 : Within hours, the barons know about the meeting and remind you of the Federal Committee's resolution. ?]

@podemos_question
title: The Podemos question
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_negotiations
view-if: podemos_talks_timer <= 0 and seeking_government = 1 and pact_up = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; podemos_talks_timer = 2

= The Podemos question

Podemos has its own incentives: it wants to overtake the PSOE, not prop it up. What do you offer Pablo Iglesias?

- @coalition: Formal talks on a coalition government
- @programme_deal: A programme agreement without ministries
- @external: A PSOE government with Podemos's external support
- @no_podemos: No government that depends on Podemos
- @easy_discard

@coalition
on-arrival: {! Q.up_talks += 1.5; Q.rel_up += 10; Q.rel_cs -= 8; Q.progressives_dissent -= 8; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 12; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 8; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 1, 0); } !}

Iglesias wants the vice-presidency and the ministries that control the economy and security. The barons want you to walk away.

@programme_deal
on-arrival: up_talks += 1; rel_up += 5; progressives_dissent -= 3; regional_leaders_dissent += 4

Podemos listens, but says a programme without power is a promise without guarantees.

@external
on-arrival: up_talks += 0.5; rel_up -= 2; sanchez_authority += 2

Podemos refuses to be "the PSOE's crutch". The offer stays on the table.

@no_podemos
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_up -= 15; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 10; Q.progressives_dissent += 10; Q.member_morale -= 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, -0.5, 0); } !}

The barons applaud. The arithmetic of any alternative to Rajoy has just become much harder.

@cs_channel
title: The Ciudadanos channel
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_negotiations
view-if: cs_talks_timer <= 0 and seeking_government = 1 and pact_cs = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; cs_talks_timer = 2

= The Ciudadanos channel

Albert Rivera signals that Ciudadanos will negotiate reforms, but never in a government that depends on Podemos.

- @bilateral: Open bilateral talks
- @three_way: Propose a three-way arrangement with Podemos
- @reform_pact: Seek a narrow pact on institutional reform
- @refuse_cs: Refuse: Ciudadanos's programme is not ours
- @easy_discard

@bilateral
on-arrival: {! Q.cs_talks += 1.5; Q.rel_cs += 10; Q.rel_up -= 8; Q.modernisers_dissent -= 5; Q.progressives_dissent += 6; Q.trade_unionists_dissent += 3; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, -0.5, 0); } !}

The two teams work fast. A document starts to take shape: 200 measures, from labour contracts to the provincial councils.

@three_way
on-arrival: cs_talks += 0.5; up_talks += 0.5; rel_cs -= 2; rel_up -= 2; sanchez_authority += 2

Both say no to sitting with the other. You have shown willing, and learned the limits.

@reform_pact
on-arrival: cs_talks += 1; rel_cs += 5; institutionalists_dissent -= 3

Anti-corruption measures, limits on political appointments. Useful, and not yet a government.

@refuse_cs
on-arrival: rel_cs -= 15; progressives_dissent -= 6; modernisers_dissent += 6

Clear lines. Fewer options.

@small_parties
title: The small parties
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_negotiations
view-if: small_parties_timer <= 0 and seeking_government = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; small_parties_timer = 2

= The small parties

Every seat counts in a second ballot, where an abstention is worth as much as a no avoided.

- @pnv_deal: The PNV: respect the Basque fiscal agreement and transfer powers
- @cc_deal: Coalición Canaria: the islands' economic regime
- @regionalists: The small regionalists: investment for their provinces
- @easy_discard

@pnv_deal
on-arrival: rel_pnv += 12; regional_leaders_dissent += 2

Aitor Esteban takes notes. The PNV never gives its vote cheaply, or early.

@cc_deal
on-arrival: rel_cc += 12

Ana Oramas will listen to any government that remembers the Canaries exist.

@regionalists
on-arrival: rel_bng += 8; rel_prc += 8; rel_te += 8; rel_geroa += 8; rel_nc += 8

A motorway here, a train line there. The small groups are pragmatic.

@party_offer
title: What does the party promise?
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: sp_negotiations
view-if: programme_timer <= 0 and seeking_government = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; programme_timer = 3

= What does the party promise?

The talks have moved from procedure to policy. Every partner wants something different. What do you lead with?

- @offer_jobs: Employment and labour rights
- @offer_pensions: Pensions and social protection
- @offer_institutions: Anti-corruption and institutional reform
- @offer_territory: Constitutional and territorial reform
- @offer_fiscal: Economic and fiscal credibility
- @easy_discard

@offer_jobs
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_up += 6; Q.rel_cs -= 4; Q.trade_unionists_dissent -= 5; Q.up_talks += 0.5; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0.5, 0); } !}

Podemos and the unions are interested. Ciudadanos wants flexibility, not rights.

@offer_pensions
on-arrival: rel_up += 3; rel_pnv += 2; rel_cc += 2; trade_unionists_dissent -= 3

Nobody objects to pensions. Nobody is won over by them either.

@offer_institutions
on-arrival: rel_cs += 6; rel_up += 3; cs_talks += 0.5; institutionalists_dissent -= 3

Common ground with both new parties: the one subject they agree on.

@offer_territory
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_pnv += 6; Q.rel_erc += 6; Q.rel_junts += 4; Q.rel_cs -= 6; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 8; Q.cat_dialogue += 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0, 1); } !}

The nationalists listen. So do the barons, with alarm.

@offer_fiscal
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_cs += 6; Q.rel_pnv += 3; Q.rel_up -= 6; Q.cs_talks += 0.5; Q.progressives_dissent += 4; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, -1, 0); } !}

Brussels would approve. Podemos calls it austerity with a red rose.
